1
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:19,100
Computer vision tracks every player in view, on the broadcast and on the pitch.

2
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:30,500
RF-DETR detects the players in view; ByteTrack follows them from frame to frame.

3
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:42,300
Each frame's camera is fitted to the painted lines: positions in pitch metres.

4
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:50,300
A pass model prices the options; a published Expected Goals (xG) model prices the shots.

5
00:00:50,400 --> 00:01:04,600
An agent newsroom on Microsoft Agent Framework, with Google Gemini, writes the line.

6
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:11,100
A fact checker ties every number to the data before it airs.

7
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:16,200
Man Utd v Man City: every option priced live, the danger zone tracked.

8
00:01:16,400 --> 00:01:19,100
Amad shoots from here: 0.06 xG.

9
00:01:19,300 --> 00:01:22,600
The pass to Mbeumo, arriving 84% of the time, was worth 0.11.

10
00:01:22,900 --> 00:01:33,000
Behind the line: agents flag it, price it, draft it, check every number, put it on air.

11
00:01:33,300 --> 00:01:37,100
Arsenal v Chelsea: Arsenal win it back through Eze.

12
00:01:37,380 --> 00:01:40,080
Eze shoots: 0.08 xG.

13
00:01:40,180 --> 00:01:43,080
The square pass, if it reaches him: 0.15 xG, arriving 66% of the time.

14
00:01:43,380 --> 00:01:44,780
Saved.

15
00:01:44,980 --> 00:01:49,780
Liverpool v Man City, 86th minute: the pass options re-price as the play moves.

16
00:01:49,880 --> 00:01:55,080
Szoboszlai shoots from 29 m: 0.02 xG. Blocked.

17
00:01:55,280 --> 00:01:59,080
Man Utd v Man City: the move into the box.

18
00:01:59,180 --> 00:02:02,780
Mbeumo from 15 m: 0.10 xG. Goal.

19
00:02:02,980 --> 00:02:06,180
Stoppage time: Cunha on the ball, Mount the best option.

20
00:02:06,280 --> 00:02:09,280
Mount shoots.

